[{"id":880968854,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOEFLz8840goSW","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I think this makes sense. I think it has been like this since the usecases of the maintainers has currently been 100% personal usage and we just have not ran into this. But I can see how it is better.\r\n\r\nMy other comments should probably be read before this, as this is the last section:\r\n\r\nHowever my main concern is the migration path.\r\n\r\nI am contemplating two relativeliy different one:\r\n\r\n1. Change the logic\r\n\r\nBy this I mean, implement the new proposed solution, allowing access between all namespaces and fixing the ACL system.\r\nAs a part of allowing access, remove the shared node code, table, tests etc.\r\n\r\nIt would be a breaking change, but we are not 1.0.0, so that \"should be fine\" :tm:.\r\n\r\n2. \"rename\" namespace to user\r\n\r\nThis is a \"even more\" breaking change, while I think it would make sense to clean up the naming to avoid confusion and bring it closer to the upstream lingo. \r\n\r\nBasically this would:\r\n- Implement the new suggestion as User (to reflect what it actually is)\r\n- Remove share node feature\r\n- Remove the namespace (cli, table, code, etc).\r\n\r\nThis would make the user/group keywords in ACLs make more sense aswell.\r\n\r\nBefore doing either, we should make sure we \"get it right\", I can't see any concerns right now, but would like to get some more eyes on it.\r\n\r\n@juanfont @madjam002 @ohdearaugustin @cure \r\n\r\nEdit:\r\nI also want to write the ACLs in YAML (as well as HUJSON), but this should be trivial.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/311#pullrequestreview-880968854","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/311","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/311#pullrequestreview-880968854"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/311"}},"submitted_at":"2022-02-13T11:43:18Z","commit_id":"7bdd7748e4cec82206369d972240363bca644527"},{"id":881045342,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOEFLz8840g69e","user":{"login":"ohdearaugustin","id":14001491,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDAxNDkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14001491?u=f13a5ed9ccb8e77059e90a8ad97d10cc3a078a56&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin","html_url":"https://github.com/ohdearaugustin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.githu